'''Aq Vetina'''<ref name="The Star Wars Book">''[[The Star Wars Book]]''</ref> was a [[planet]]<ref name="Encyclopedia">{{EncyclopediaCite|Din Djarin and Other Characters of the Underworld}}</ref> inhabited by a number of [[human]]s. During the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] [[Attack on Aq Vetina|attacked]] a settlement on the planet, [[Death|killing]] the population. The [[Mandalorian]]s of [[Death Watch]] intervened in the attack, fighting back against the Separatist [[Separatist Droid Army|droid forces]].<ref name="Chapter 8" /> Aq Vetina was the [[homeworld]] of<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> the young human [[Din Djarin]], who was rescued from the attack by a [[Unidentified Mandalorian warrior|Mandalorian warrior]] and raised as a [[foundling]] in the [[Mandalorian Creed]].<ref name="Chapter 8" />

{{Planet-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Aq Vetina first appeared is in a flashback in episode of the television series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'', which was titled "[[Chapter 1: The Mandalorian]]"<ref name="Chapter 1">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}}</ref> and aired on [[November 12]], [[2019]].<ref name="Episode Amount">{{WebCite|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/star-wars-new-mandalorian-details-footage-unveiled-1201931|text='The Mandalorian': Jon Favreau Teases Disney+ Series at Star Wars Celebration|author=Aaron Couch & Graeme McMillan|date=2018-12-10|archivedate=20191109001233}}</ref>

